{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>They drip</b> — behold, Your circuits are in the settled land." "<b>Pastures of the wilderness</b> — like: נות רועים (pastures of shepherds)." "<b>And the hills gird themselves with gladness</b> — when the grass and herbage appear."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {0 "Reading מעגליך as 'Your circuits'; the argument is compressed and the point is not expanded."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:46.682679417Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}